01. PROJECT OBJECTIVE

Build a fully functional, production-oriented native Android application called SYMPHINE GAME SPACE, developed by Reo Moser.

This application must be a complete Android Gaming Center inspired by the functionality and experience of gaming platforms such as Nubia RedMagic Gaming Space, ASUS ROG Gaming Center, Realme Game Space, POCO Game Turbo and modern gaming dashboards, but with original Symphine design, architecture, features and implementation.

The application must not be a website, WebView application, HTML prototype, visual mockup, fake dashboard or non-functional UI.

The project must contain real Kotlin source code, real Android APIs, actual application navigation, actual data, permission management, monitoring, local persistence, configuration management, compatibility detection, error handling and a working Android APK whenever the build environment allows.

<text color="success" weight="semibold">Priority: Functional implementation over feature count. Never simulate a successful system operation.</text>

Core objectives

- Create a premium Android gaming management application.
- Automatically detect installed games.
- Provide individual Game Detail Centers for installed games.
- Implement real Android device monitoring.
- Implement supported display controls.
- Implement safe and reversible system configuration.
- Provide optional Shizuku integration.
- Provide per-game customization and profile management.
- Provide offline recommendation engine.
- Implement real backup and restore.
- Implement actual permission handling.
- Support devices with different manufacturers, chipsets and Android versions.
- Build an installable APK rather than stopping at source code or screenshots.

