02. STRICT DEVELOPMENT RULES

The developer or AI coding agent MUST follow these rules:

1. Implement real functionality using native Android APIs.
2. Never use WebView as the main application interface.
3. Never fabricate monitoring data.
4. Never display random CPU, RAM, GPU, temperature or FPS values.
5. Never claim a system setting was successfully applied without verification.
6. Never create buttons that do nothing.
7. Never display fake FPS improvements or fake performance scores.
8. Never claim universal Android compatibility.
9. Never automatically modify undocumented system properties in bulk.
10. Never disable Android thermal protection, security mechanisms or system-critical functionality.
11. Never modify game files, game memory, game internals or anti-cheat systems.
12. Never implement cheats, aim assist, auto-targeting, macros or gameplay manipulation.
13. Never force-stop critical system applications.
14. Never aggressively kill background applications.
15. Never automatically delete user files.
16. Never execute arbitrary commands generated from user input.
17. Never require root for core application functionality.
18. Shizuku must remain optional.
19. If an API is inaccessible, display Unsupported, Unknown or Requires Permission.
20. Every supported system modification must have validation, confirmation, backup when possible, verification and rollback.
21. UI customization must not be confused with system configuration.
22. All stored personal configurations must remain local unless the user explicitly exports them.
23. Do not introduce unnecessary internet dependencies.
24. Do not implement placeholder functionality merely to satisfy a feature list.
25. Document all limitations clearly.

